% composition-series: Ontario Listening Bridges — set 1
% composition-grade: 8
% composition-elements: major and minor tonality, heard as a journey: E minor (bars 1-4), G major (bars 5-8), E minor turning to E major at the last chord (bars 9-12); the three textures in order, one per scene: monophonic (the theme alone, bars 1-4), homophonic (a second line moving in the same rhythm in thirds and sixths over chords, bars 5-8), polyphonic (a running eighth-note line against the second line's half notes, bars 9-12); form for a dramatic purpose, an assembly that gathers: alone, together, interwoven, arrived; arranging for mixed ensemble with two written lines plus chords
% composition-listen: A. R. Rahman — "Jai Ho" (featuring Sukhwinder Singh, Tanvi Shah and Mahalakshmi Iyer; lyrics by Gulzar), from Slumdog Millionaire (Music From the Motion Picture), 2008
% composition-listen-url: https://music.apple.com/us/song/jai-ho-feat-sukhwinder-singh-tanvi-shah-mahalakshmi-iyer/1443885535
% composition-bridge: Hear how percussion, voices, strings, electronic production and sectional buildup serve a cinematic arc.
% composition-context: A. R. Rahman's film work can open study of Indian cinema, multilingual song, studio production and global circulation. This new ensemble theme is not a Bollywood imitation or a "Jai Ho" arrangement.
% composition-distance: Original melody, second line, form and harmony; no hook, rhythm, vocal, lyric, sample or orchestration from the recording is copied.
